1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,263
Your app runs on your laptop,

2
00:00:02,263 --> 00:00:03,296
on a test server,

3
00:00:03,296 --> 00:00:04,391
and in production.

4
00:00:04,391 --> 00:00:04,999
Same code,

5
00:00:04,999 --> 00:00:06,397
three different places.

6
00:00:06,397 --> 00:00:08,585
How does it know which one it is in?

7
00:00:09,135 --> 00:00:13,893
If you edit the code for each place, you will ship the wrong settings, sooner or later.

8
00:00:14,443 --> 00:00:17,199
Today you learn four ideas: configuration,

9
00:00:17,199 --> 00:00:19,102
which lives outside the code.

10
00:00:19,102 --> 00:00:20,546
Environment variables,

11
00:00:20,546 --> 00:00:21,727
which override it.

12
00:00:21,727 --> 00:00:22,646
Feature flags,

13
00:00:22,646 --> 00:00:24,811
which switch features on and off.

14
00:00:24,811 --> 00:00:25,730
And fail fast,

15
00:00:25,730 --> 00:00:28,224
which stops a bad setting at the door.

16
00:00:28,774 --> 00:00:32,465
Change behaviour, without changing code. That is the whole trick.

17
00:00:34,515 --> 00:00:37,630
Go into the shop. Type: CD, cloud cart.

18
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:41,230
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

19
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:46,154
This version has a settings file. Show it. Type: cat, app dot conf.

20
00:00:46,704 --> 00:00:47,526
Plain text.

21
00:00:47,526 --> 00:00:47,825
Key,

22
00:00:47,825 --> 00:00:48,348
equals,

23
00:00:48,348 --> 00:00:48,797
value.

24
00:00:48,797 --> 00:00:49,544
A comment,

25
00:00:49,544 --> 00:00:50,516
a store name,

26
00:00:50,516 --> 00:00:51,637
and a currency.

27
00:00:51,637 --> 00:00:52,235
No code,

28
00:00:52,235 --> 00:00:53,879
so anyone can read it,

29
00:00:53,879 --> 00:00:56,794
and nobody needs to recompile anything.

30
00:00:57,344 --> 00:01:00,933
Now ask the running API what it actually uses.

31
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:01,792
Type: curl,

32
00:01:01,792 --> 00:01:02,338
dash s,

33
00:01:02,338 --> 00:01:03,274
the address,

34
00:01:03,274 --> 00:01:05,069
slash API slash config,

35
00:01:05,069 --> 00:01:05,459
pipe,

36
00:01:05,459 --> 00:01:05,771
J Q.

37
00:01:07,321 --> 00:01:08,673
Look at the brackets.

38
00:01:08,673 --> 00:01:11,700
Store name and currency come from app dot conf.

39
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:14,211
But port and flag discount say default.

40
00:01:14,211 --> 00:01:15,241
Nobody set them,

41
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:17,881
so the value written in the code is used.

42
00:01:18,431 --> 00:01:21,299
So there are three layers: the default in the code,

43
00:01:21,299 --> 00:01:22,312
the settings file,

44
00:01:22,312 --> 00:01:22,537
and,

45
00:01:22,537 --> 00:01:23,718
as you will see next,

46
00:01:23,718 --> 00:01:24,618
the environment.

47
00:01:26,668 --> 00:01:30,593
Same shop, new session. Go in. Type: CD, cloud cart.

48
00:01:31,143 --> 00:01:35,255
An environment variable is a setting you hand to one program,

49
00:01:35,255 --> 00:01:36,468
when you start it.

50
00:01:36,468 --> 00:01:38,895
Put the variable before the command.

51
00:01:38,895 --> 00:01:40,513
Type: store name equals,

52
00:01:40,513 --> 00:01:41,861
blue shop in quotes,

53
00:01:41,861 --> 00:01:43,815
then dot slash start dot S H.

54
00:01:45,865 --> 00:01:51,241
Nothing in the code changed. Nothing in app dot conf changed. Ask the API again.

55
00:01:51,791 --> 00:01:53,656
Same command as before.

56
00:01:53,656 --> 00:01:54,548
Type: curl,

57
00:01:54,548 --> 00:01:55,115
dash s,

58
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:56,088
the address,

59
00:01:56,088 --> 00:01:57,952
slash API slash config,

60
00:01:57,952 --> 00:01:58,358
pipe,

61
00:01:58,358 --> 00:01:58,682
J Q.

62
00:02:00,232 --> 00:02:00,885
Blue Shop,

63
00:02:00,885 --> 00:02:03,041
and the bracket says environment.

64
00:02:03,041 --> 00:02:05,653
The environment beats the settings file.

65
00:02:05,653 --> 00:02:08,266
That is the order of power: environment,

66
00:02:08,266 --> 00:02:08,919
then file,

67
00:02:08,919 --> 00:02:09,768
then default.

68
00:02:10,318 --> 00:02:13,304
The variable lived only for that one start.

69
00:02:13,304 --> 00:02:15,318
Start again with no variable.

70
00:02:15,318 --> 00:02:17,401
Type: dot slash start dot S H.

71
00:02:19,451 --> 00:02:21,709
Check the store name once more.

72
00:02:21,709 --> 00:02:22,510
Type: curl,

73
00:02:22,510 --> 00:02:23,020
dash s,

74
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:24,403
the config address,

75
00:02:24,403 --> 00:02:24,768
pipe,

76
00:02:24,768 --> 00:02:25,059
J Q,

77
00:02:25,059 --> 00:02:25,569
dash R,

78
00:02:25,569 --> 00:02:26,661
dot store name.

79
00:02:27,211 --> 00:02:28,691
Back to the file value.

80
00:02:28,691 --> 00:02:29,527
Same program,

81
00:02:29,527 --> 00:02:30,170
same file,

82
00:02:30,170 --> 00:02:31,586
different environment,

83
00:02:31,586 --> 00:02:32,872
different behaviour.

84
00:02:32,872 --> 00:02:35,574
That is how one build runs in every place.

85
00:02:37,624 --> 00:02:40,739
Go into the shop. Type: CD, cloud cart.

86
00:02:41,289 --> 00:02:44,339
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

87
00:02:44,889 --> 00:02:49,504
Now a feature flag: a setting that turns a feature on or off.

88
00:02:49,504 --> 00:02:49,958
First,

89
00:02:49,958 --> 00:02:52,378
how does product one look today?

90
00:02:52,378 --> 00:02:53,210
Type: curl,

91
00:02:53,210 --> 00:02:53,740
dash s,

92
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:55,329
the products address,

93
00:02:55,329 --> 00:02:55,707
pipe,

94
00:02:55,707 --> 00:02:56,009
J Q,

95
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:56,539
dash C,

96
00:02:56,539 --> 00:02:56,842
dot,

97
00:02:56,842 --> 00:02:57,447
bracket,

98
00:02:57,447 --> 00:02:57,825
zero,

99
00:02:57,825 --> 00:02:58,884
close bracket.

100
00:03:00,434 --> 00:03:02,810
The backpack costs thirty-nine dollars.

101
00:03:02,810 --> 00:03:05,735
The new discount feature is already in the code,

102
00:03:05,735 --> 00:03:06,953
but the flag is off,

103
00:03:06,953 --> 00:03:08,050
so nobody sees it.

104
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:09,524
Switch it on,

105
00:03:09,524 --> 00:03:10,731
with no new code.

106
00:03:10,731 --> 00:03:12,152
Start with the flag.

107
00:03:12,152 --> 00:03:14,284
Type: flag discount equals on,

108
00:03:14,284 --> 00:03:16,344
then dot slash start dot S H.

109
00:03:18,394 --> 00:03:21,317
Look at the backpack again. Same command as before.

110
00:03:23,667 --> 00:03:26,995
Thirty-five ten. Ten percent off. The feature is live.

111
00:03:27,545 --> 00:03:29,335
This is why teams love flags.

112
00:03:29,335 --> 00:03:31,742
You can ship code that is switched off,

113
00:03:31,742 --> 00:03:33,223
turn it on for everyone,

114
00:03:33,223 --> 00:03:35,137
or turn it back off in seconds,

115
00:03:35,137 --> 00:03:36,371
if something breaks.

116
00:03:36,371 --> 00:03:39,705
Deploying and releasing become two separate decisions.

117
00:03:41,755 --> 00:03:44,870
Go into the shop. Type: CD, cloud cart.

118
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:47,881
What if someone sets a bad value?

119
00:03:47,881 --> 00:03:49,522
Start the API by hand,

120
00:03:49,522 --> 00:03:51,983
with a port that is not a number.

121
00:03:51,983 --> 00:03:53,774
Type: port equals A B C,

122
00:03:53,774 --> 00:03:54,743
python three,

123
00:03:54,743 --> 00:03:55,638
API dot P Y.

124
00:03:57,688 --> 00:03:59,008
It refuses to start,

125
00:03:59,008 --> 00:04:02,109
and it says exactly why: port must be a number,

126
00:04:02,109 --> 00:04:02,769
got A B C.

127
00:04:02,769 --> 00:04:03,626
Failing fast,

128
00:04:03,626 --> 00:04:05,012
with a clear message,

129
00:04:05,012 --> 00:04:07,651
is far better than starting half broken.

130
00:04:08,201 --> 00:04:11,764
Check how it ended. Type: echo, dollar, question mark.

131
00:04:12,314 --> 00:04:13,206
Exit code one.

132
00:04:13,206 --> 00:04:15,690
Anything other than zero means failure,

133
00:04:15,690 --> 00:04:18,557
and that is what lets a deploy pipeline stop.

134
00:04:18,557 --> 00:04:20,724
Validate your settings at startup,

135
00:04:20,724 --> 00:04:21,743
and never guess.

136
00:04:23,793 --> 00:04:25,478
Let us put the ideas together.

137
00:04:26,028 --> 00:04:30,812
Configuration: settings that differ between places belong outside the code.

138
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:31,259
A file,

139
00:04:31,259 --> 00:04:32,471
or the environment.

140
00:04:33,021 --> 00:04:35,903
Order of power: the environment beats the file,

141
00:04:35,903 --> 00:04:37,804
and the file beats the default.

142
00:04:37,804 --> 00:04:39,582
Learn the order of your tool,

143
00:04:39,582 --> 00:04:41,789
because it decides which value wins.

144
00:04:42,339 --> 00:04:43,687
Same build everywhere.

145
00:04:43,687 --> 00:04:44,606
You build once,

146
00:04:44,606 --> 00:04:46,935
then run it in test and in production,

147
00:04:46,935 --> 00:04:48,405
with different settings.

148
00:04:48,405 --> 00:04:50,979
This idea is called the twelve factor app.

149
00:04:51,529 --> 00:04:53,944
Feature flags: ship code switched off,

150
00:04:53,944 --> 00:04:55,659
release by flipping a flag,

151
00:04:55,659 --> 00:04:57,819
and roll back by flipping it back.

152
00:04:57,819 --> 00:04:58,900
Remove old flags,

153
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:00,361
so they do not pile up.

154
00:05:00,911 --> 00:05:02,859
Secrets are configuration too,

155
00:05:02,859 --> 00:05:05,977
but special: they never go in the settings file,

156
00:05:05,977 --> 00:05:07,081
and never in git.

157
00:05:07,081 --> 00:05:09,679
Use a private file or a secrets manager.

158
00:05:10,229 --> 00:05:14,944
And fail fast. Check every setting at startup, and refuse to run with a bad one.

159
00:05:15,494 --> 00:05:16,610
In real systems,

160
00:05:16,610 --> 00:05:17,866
tools like docker,

161
00:05:17,866 --> 00:05:18,633
kubernetes,

162
00:05:18,633 --> 00:05:21,773
and the cloud inject these variables for you.

163
00:05:21,773 --> 00:05:24,006
The idea stays exactly the same.

164
00:05:26,056 --> 00:05:28,829
Your task, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

165
00:05:29,379 --> 00:05:31,930
The lab is lab seventy-one dot S H,

166
00:05:31,930 --> 00:05:35,648
in the academy slash lab folder of git hub dot com,

167
00:05:35,648 --> 00:05:37,106
slash it dash waves,

168
00:05:37,106 --> 00:05:38,782
slash dev ops dash A I.

169
00:05:38,782 --> 00:05:40,458
Install it like before,

170
00:05:40,458 --> 00:05:41,625
then run lab up,

171
00:05:41,625 --> 00:05:45,123
and work inside slash opt slash lab seventy-one.

172
00:05:45,673 --> 00:05:50,518
One: start the API with store name set to Blue Shop in the environment,

173
00:05:50,518 --> 00:05:53,588
and save the config answer in E N V dot text.

174
00:05:54,138 --> 00:05:59,450
Two: start it with the discount flag on, and save the products answer in flag dot text.

175
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,062
Three: start the API by hand with a bad port,

176
00:06:03,062 --> 00:06:06,056
and write the exit code in answers dot text,

177
00:06:06,056 --> 00:06:07,484
like this: fail fast,

178
00:06:07,484 --> 00:06:07,893
colon,

179
00:06:07,893 --> 00:06:08,981
then the number.

180
00:06:09,531 --> 00:06:14,971
Four: change the currency in app dot conf to E U R, and restart with no variables.

181
00:06:15,521 --> 00:06:20,151
Five: do all of it without editing a single line of API dot P Y.

182
00:06:20,701 --> 00:06:23,239
Then run lab check. Five pass lines.

183
00:06:25,289 --> 00:06:27,273
Six points, and you need all six.

184
00:06:27,823 --> 00:06:29,700
The checker shows five pass lines.

185
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:32,810
You can explain why settings live outside the code.

186
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:36,966
You can give the order of power: environment, file, default.

187
00:06:37,516 --> 00:06:41,548
You can explain a feature flag, and why it separates deploy from release.

188
00:06:42,098 --> 00:06:45,020
You can explain fail fast, and read an exit code.

189
00:06:45,570 --> 00:06:48,301
You ran lab down, and nothing is left listening.

190
00:06:48,851 --> 00:06:50,472
To pass, you need all six.

191
00:06:52,522 --> 00:06:55,359
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

192
00:06:55,909 --> 00:06:58,128
One: install the lab, and run lab up.

193
00:06:58,678 --> 00:07:01,707
Two: override the store name, and save the config.

194
00:07:02,257 --> 00:07:04,924
Three: switch on the flag, and save the products.

195
00:07:05,474 --> 00:07:08,013
Four: break the port, and write the exit code.

196
00:07:08,563 --> 00:07:11,400
Five: set the currency in the file, then restart.

197
00:07:11,950 --> 00:07:14,233
Six: run lab check, then lab down.

198
00:07:14,783 --> 00:07:16,617
Pause the video, and begin now.

199
00:07:32,167 --> 00:07:33,042
Quick check.

200
00:07:33,592 --> 00:07:36,962
Which wins: the environment, the settings file, or the default?

201
00:07:37,512 --> 00:07:40,670
How do you switch a feature on without deploying new code?

202
00:07:41,220 --> 00:07:44,334
Why is the same build in every environment a good idea?

203
00:07:44,884 --> 00:07:47,786
What should a program do when it is given a bad setting?

204
00:07:48,336 --> 00:07:50,812
Objective covered: M C zero eight,

205
00:07:50,812 --> 00:07:52,996
objective five: configuration,

206
00:07:52,996 --> 00:07:54,598
environment variables,

207
00:07:54,598 --> 00:07:55,909
and feature flags.

208
00:07:56,459 --> 00:07:58,528
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

209
